Description
===========
Fixes: ⏳ Draining 1 active agent(s) before restart... hanging indefinitely

Root cause
----------
1. deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash via Nous hits HTTP 429 (rate limited)
2. Fallback stepfun/step-3.7-flash:free via Nous ALSO hits HTTP 429
3. conversation_loop retries 3x with no exponential backoff
4. Stuck agent never resolves → drain never completes → /restart hangs forever

Fix summary
-----------
Three new env vars injected via entrypoint.sh BEFORE `exec hermes gateway run`:

  HERMES_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30
    Hard kill agents still alive after N seconds during drain.
    Prevents infinite /restart hangs. Hermes reads this natively.

  HERMES_RATE_LIMIT_BACKOFF_BASE=2
    Base multiplier for exponential backoff on RateLimitError (seconds).
    Retry 1: ~2s, Retry 2: ~4s, Retry 3: ~8s.

  HERMES_RATE_LIMIT_MAX_RETRIES=2
    Reduce max retries from 3 to 2 on rate-limited providers to fail
    faster and let the drain complete.

Apply
-----
This patch documents the env var additions. The actual change is in
entrypoint.sh — see the section '── Rate-limit resilience & drain timeout'
added before 'exec hermes gateway run'.

To apply manually in entrypoint.sh, add before the final exec line:

  # ── Rate-limit resilience & drain timeout ───────────────────────────────
  # Fixes: /restart hangs when Nous rate-limits both primary and fallback model.
  # HERMES_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS: hard-kill agents still alive after N seconds.
  # HERMES_RATE_LIMIT_BACKOFF_BASE: exponential backoff base in seconds.
  # HERMES_RATE_LIMIT_MAX_RETRIES: max retries on 429 (lower = faster drain).
  export HERMES_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS="${HERMES_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:-30}"
  export HERMES_RATE_LIMIT_BACKOFF_BASE="${HERMES_RATE_LIMIT_BACKOFF_BASE:-2}"
  export HERMES_RATE_LIMIT_MAX_RETRIES="${HERMES_RATE_LIMIT_MAX_RETRIES:-2}"
  echo "   Rate-limit resilience: backoff_base=${HERMES_RATE_LIMIT_BACKOFF_BASE}s, max_retries=${HERMES_RATE_LIMIT_MAX_RETRIES}, drain_timeout=${HERMES_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS}s"

Verification
------------
1. After deploy: /restart should complete within 30 seconds
2. Logs should show 'Rate-limit resilience: backoff_base=2s ...'
3. On 429: logs show retry delays (2s, 4s) instead of instant retry storm
4. Drain no longer blocks indefinitely

